# What EAS Build does not need uploaded.
#
# This file belongs HERE, at the git repository root, and nowhere else.
#
# An earlier attempt put it in `ranna-bari/User and Cook App/` beside app.json
# and eas.json, which is where you would expect it to go and where it does
# nothing at all. EAS CLI builds its archive "starting from the root of the
# git repository", and it reads `.easignore` from that same root — so the copy
# in the app folder was never opened, and the build uploaded 594 MB: the whole
# repository, including the node_modules of all three projects.
#
# Because the archive starts here rather than at the app, the rules have to
# cover every project in the repository, not just the one being built.
#
# When this file is present, EAS ignores every .gitignore in the repository.
# That is why the entries below repeat things the individual projects already
# ignore for themselves: from EAS's point of view those files no longer exist.
#
# Rule of thumb for anything added later: exclude it if the build server can
# regenerate it or never reads it, and keep it if the build reads it.

# Installed on the builder from each project's lockfile. This is nearly all of
# the 594 MB.
node_modules/

# Build output and caches, all regenerable.
.expo/
dist/
web-build/
.next/
out/
build/
.turbo/
.metro-health-check*
*.tsbuildinfo
expo-env.d.ts

# Generated by prebuild on the builder itself.
/ranna-bari/User and Cook App/ios
/ranna-bari/User and Cook App/android
.kotlin/

# Static design reference. Not an input to any build.
/html css design/

# Scratch directories from headless-browser verification runs.
.smoke/
.exportcheck/
.expo-export-check/
.claude/

# Secrets never belong in a build archive. Build-time configuration goes in
# eas.json under the profile's `env`, which is where EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL is.
.env
.env.*
*.jks
*.keystore
*.p8
*.p12
*.key
*.pem
